It is completely reliable if done correctly. Don't look for "moves only
reluctantly", look for its absence; if a pet steps on an item, was not
going to eat food on that spot, was not displaced, and did not move
reluctantly, the item on that spot is not cursed.

Of course if the pet does move reluctantly, you know the item is cursed -
but more likely you will simply have an item that the pet avoids and
strongly suspect it was cursed.

I don't know why JoaoSantos did not take account of pet-testing.

